---
import AdminNav from '../../components/AdminNav.astro';
import '@fontsource/sora/400.css';
import '@fontsource/sora/600.css';
import '../../styles/seo-quick-wins.css';
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow"/><title>SEO Quick Wins | NC Digital Admin</title></head><body>
<AdminNav />
<header><a href="/admin/links/" class="brand">SEO Quick Wins</a></header>
<main><div class="intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">GOOGLE SEARCH CONSOLE · CLIENT OPPORTUNITIES</p><h1>Find the next move.<br/><span>Use the evidence you have.</span></h1><p>Turn your clients’ search performance into a prioritised list of pages to improve.</p></div><div class="connection"><span id="connection">Connecting to Google…</span><button id="reconnect" type="button">Refresh connection</button></div></div>
<section class="panel search-panel"><form id="research-form"><fieldset id="fields"><div class="search-grid"><label>Client / Search Console property<select id="site" required><option value="">Loading accessible properties…</option></select></label><label>Compare periods<select id="days"><option value="28">28 days vs previous 28</option><option value="56">56 days vs previous 56</option><option value="84">84 days vs previous 84</option></select></label><button id="start" class="primary" disabled>Find quick wins ↗</button></div><details class="options"><summary>Country, device and opportunity thresholds</summary><div class="options-grid"><label>Country<select id="country"><option value="gbr">United Kingdom</option><option value="all">All countries</option></select></label><label>Device<select id="device"><option value="all">All devices</option><option value="MOBILE">Mobile</option><option value="DESKTOP">Desktop</option><option value="TABLET">Tablet</option></select></label><label>Minimum keyword impressions<input id="impressions" type="number" min="10" max="100000" value="50"/></label><label>Low CTR threshold (%)<input id="ctr" type="number" min="0.1" max="20" step="0.1" value="2"/></label><label class="wide">Exclude brand terms from keyword opportunities<input id="brands" maxlength="800" placeholder="Optional · e.g. nc digital, ncdigital"/></label></div></details><div class="search-meta"><span>Finalised data · latest 3 days excluded · no DataForSEO credits</span><label><input type="checkbox" id="fresh"/> Refresh saved data</label></div></fieldset></form></section>
<div id="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></div>
<div class="saved"><label for="saved">Saved research</label><select id="saved"><option value="">Choose a report…</option></select><button id="open">Open report</button></div>
<section class="panel progress" id="progress" hidden><div><p class="eyebrow">RESEARCH PROGRESS</p><h2 id="phase"></h2><p id="progress-copy"></p></div><div class="actions"><button id="resume" hidden>Resume</button><button id="stop">Stop</button></div></section>
<section id="empty" class="empty"><div class="empty-icon">↗</div><h2>Know which pages deserve your next hour.</h2><div class="features"><div><span>01</span><h3>Within reach</h3><p>Find queries with impressions and average positions 5–20.</p></div><div><span>02</span><h3>Missing clicks</h3><p>Investigate low click-through and pages losing search traffic.</p></div><div><span>03</span><h3>A practical work list</h3><p>Review the evidence, choose an action and track what you change.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="report" hidden><div class="report-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR OPPORTUNITY REPORT</p><h2 id="title"></h2><p id="dates"></p></div><div class="actions"><button id="export">Export opportunities</button><button id="print">Print work plan</button></div></div><div id="warnings"></div><div class="stats" id="stats"></div>
<div class="overview"><section class="panel"><div class="section-heading"><h3>Daily search clicks</h3><span>Previous period → current period</span></div><div id="trend"></div></section><section class="panel recommendation"><p class="eyebrow">WHERE TO START</p><h3 id="recommendation-title"></h3><p id="recommendation-copy"></p></section></div>
<div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Research views"><button id="opportunities-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="opportunities-panel" data-tab="opportunities">Keyword & page signals</button><button id="pages-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="pages-panel" tabindex="-1" data-tab="pages">Page work plan</button><button id="coverage-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="coverage-panel" tabindex="-1" data-tab="coverage">Coverage & missing data</button></div>
<section id="opportunities-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="opportunities-tab"><div class="filters"><input type="search" id="search" placeholder="Filter by keyword or page…" aria-label="Filter opportunities"/><select id="type" aria-label="Opportunity type"><option value="all">All signals</option><option value="striking-distance">Positions 5–20</option><option value="low-ctr">Low CTR</option><option value="declining-page">Declining page</option><option value="lost-position">Lost position</option></select><select id="sort" aria-label="Sort opportunities"><option value="score">Sort: priority</option><option value="impressions">Sort: impressions</option><option value="clicks">Sort: clicks</option></select><span id="count"></span></div><p class="hint">Impressions are appearances of this website in search, not monthly keyword search volume. Position is an average. One page can have several signals.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Keyword / page</th><th>Signal</th><th>Impressions</th><th>Clicks</th><th>CTR</th><th>Avg. position</th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody id="rows"></tbody></table></div><p id="no-results" class="empty-small" hidden>No opportunities match these filters.</p></section>
<section id="pages-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="pages-tab" hidden><p class="hint">Each page has one work item. Page totals come from a separate page-level Google query; overlapping keyword impressions are not added together.</p><div class="page-controls"><label>Work status<select id="status-filter"><option value="active">Active work</option><option value="all">All pages</option><option value="done">Done</option><option value="dismissed">Dismissed</option></select></label><span id="page-count"></span></div><div id="page-plans" class="page-plans"></div></section>
<section id="coverage-panel" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="coverage-tab" hidden><div class="panel" id="coverage"></div><div id="missing"></div></section>
<details class="panel methodology"><summary>How opportunities are chosen</summary><p>Positions 5–20 are a screening range. Low CTR means below your selected threshold with at least 100 impressions and an average position of 10 or better. A declining page needs at least 10 previous clicks, a decline of 20% or more and at least five fewer clicks. Lost-position signals need at least a two-position deterioration, fewer clicks and sufficient impressions in both periods.</p><p>Priority combines impression volume, signal type and average position. It is a transparent sorting heuristic, not a Google score or a forecast. “More evidence” means at least 200 impressions; it is not a statistical significance test. Brand exclusions affect keyword signals; property totals and declining-page signals still include branded searches.</p><p>Both date ranges have equal length and do not overlap. Google’s reporting dates use Pacific time. The latest three days are excluded and only finalised data is requested. Seasonality, search features and query mix can change clicks and average position without a technical SEO problem.</p><p>Search Console can omit anonymised queries and returns top rows rather than an exhaustive dataset. Each detailed dataset is capped at 5,000 returned rows. Missing rows are not assumed to have zero traffic. Reports are reused for 24 hours when the selected periods and filters match.</p><p><a href="https://developers.google.com/webmaster-tools/v1/searchanalytics/query" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google’s data definitions and limitations ↗</a></p></details>
</section></main><dialog id="detail"><div class="dialog-heading"><p class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE & NEXT ACTION</p><button id="close" aria-label="Close details">✕</button></div><div id="detail-body"></div></dialog><script>import '../../scripts/seo-quick-wins.js';</script></body></html>
